From 47cc53a973857ea51847d6a3ae9accdf1e7fd19c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:54:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] BananaDS: melonDS patch 0024 (jit.entry_x26):
 ARM_Dispatch sets x26, blocks have no entry prologue

0007's FASTENTRY prologue (2-4 instructions setting the fast memory base in x26 at every block's start, run only
when the loop dispatches the block) moves into ARM_Dispatch, which now gets the base as an argument. Every block
is 12 bytes smaller: on tests/bigcode (a game-sized code footprint) the JIT's code is ~4% smaller and rgds-sim
gives the main thread -1.7% (L1I misses to DRAM -4.6%); cpubench-thumb -0.3%. Exact (pictures, main RAM and audio
identical with it off and on); jit.entry_x26=off (MELONDS_JIT_NOENTRYX26=1) keeps the prologue.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
