 | `jit.codegen` | `new` | melonDS's JIT's code generation (patches/melonds/0007): `new` (fewer host instructions per block and per exit: cheaper exit stubs, linkable exits both ways of a block-ending branch, self loops checked inline, host flags kept in NZCV, a per-site cache for returns) or `old` (the code before 0007, byte for byte). Exact either way. Sets `MELONDS_JIT_OLDCODEGEN`; each part is also off alone with its `MELONDS_JIT_NO<name>=1` (docs/PERF.md lists them). `MELONDS_JIT_NOFASTLDM=1` keeps block loads (LDM, POP) off the fastmem path (0008). `MELONDS_JIT_LOOPREGS=1` turns on loops that keep their guest registers in host registers (off: HeartGold hangs with it, docs/PERF.md) |
 | `jit.hugepages` | `on` | the JIT's 32 MB code memory aligned to 2 MB and `madvise(MADV_HUGEPAGE)`'d before its first use, so a kernel with transparent huge pages in `madvise` mode (BananaLinux) maps it with 2 MB pages: fewer iTLB misses and page walks on the A55 (patches/melonds/0021). Emulation doesn't change. Sets `MELONDS_JIT_HUGEPAGE`, read as the first JIT starts; the log line `[jit] code memory at ..., N kB on huge pages` says what the kernel gave |
 | `jit.irqchain` | `on` | a chain of linked JIT blocks goes on past an IRQ that CPSR.I masks, instead of going back to the loop at every block exit while one is pending (melonDS sets its IRQ flag whatever CPSR.I is; the loop's TriggerIRQ would do nothing with it) (patches/melonds/0023). Exact. `off` sets `MELONDS_JIT_NOIRQCHAIN=1`; `jit.codegen=old` turns it off too. `MELONDS_JIT_EXITSTATS=n` (0022) prints at exit, per frame from frame n on, why chains came back to the loop: compiles, region setups, IRQs taken, IRQs masked, halts and idle loops |
+| `jit.entry_x26` | `on` | melonDS's ARM_Dispatch puts the CPU's fast memory base in x26, so the JIT's blocks have no entry prologue (12 bytes less per block, three instructions less per dispatch) (patches/melonds/0024). Exact. `off` sets `MELONDS_JIT_NOENTRYX26=1`; `jit.codegen=old` turns it off too |
 | `jit.iofast` | `on` | direct routes for the JIT's slow memory paths: main RAM block transfers, VRAM, the GX FIFO and command ports, IE/IF/IME/DISPSTAT/VCOUNT/KEYINPUT reads (patches/melonds/0005). Exact. Sets `MELONDS_IOFAST`; `MELONDS_IOFAST_ROUTES` picks single routes, `MELONDS_IOSTATS=n` prints the slow accesses by address from frame n |
 | `jit.vramfast` | `on` | VRAM with one bank at a 16 KB page written and read straight to the bank (with the dirty bit and the capture check), OAM and palette straight to the GPU (patches/melonds/0010). Exact. Bit 1 of `MELONDS_MEMFAST` |
 | `jit.iodirect` | `on` | the divider, square root, IPCSYNC/IPCFIFOCNT, the IPC FIFOs and IME/IE/IF read and written straight to their state, other IO registers without the ARM9Read*/ARM7Read* dispatch, one function per hot register for the JIT's static-address calls (patches/melonds/0010). Exact. Bit 2 of `MELONDS_MEMFAST` |
diff --git a/bananads/patches/melonds/0024-ARMJIT_A64-ARM_Dispatch-sets-x26-blocks-have-no-entr.patch b/bananads/patches/melonds/0024-ARMJIT_A64-ARM_Dispatch-sets-x26-blocks-have-no-entr.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..14620b9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bananads/patches/melonds/0024-ARMJIT_A64-ARM_Dispatch-sets-x26-blocks-have-no-entr.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,157 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
+Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:42:48 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] ARMJIT_A64: ARM_Dispatch sets x26, blocks have no entry
+ prologue (MELONDS_JIT_NOENTRYX26)
+
+0007's FASTENTRY put the fast memory base into x26 with a 2-4 instruction prologue at every block's start,
+which the loop's ARM_Dispatch entered and linked exits skipped. ARM_Dispatch now takes the base as a third
+argument (ARMJIT_Memory::FastMemStart(num)) and sets x26 itself, so blocks have no prologue at all: 12 bytes less
+per block (on tests/bigcode, ~6% of the JIT's code) and three instructions less per dispatch. Everything else that
+enters a block (a linked slot, DynExit, a self loop, the fault handler's context restore) comes from code of the
+same CPU, where x26 already holds it. MELONDS_JIT_NOENTRYX26=1 (or jit.codegen=old) keeps the prologue; x26 is
+then set twice on a dispatch, as harmless as before.
+---
+ src/ARM.cpp                        | 4 ++--
+ src/ARMJIT.h                       | 5 +++--
+ src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp | 8 ++++++--
+ src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h   | 2 ++
+ src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Linkage.S    | 3 ++-
+ src/ARMJIT_Memory.h                | 2 ++
+ src/NDS.cpp                        | 2 +-
+ 7 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/src/ARM.cpp b/src/ARM.cpp
+index 3937a99..9c5b8e4 100644
+--- a/src/ARM.cpp
++++ b/src/ARM.cpp
+@@ -632,7 +632,7 @@ void ARMv5::Execute()
+             JitBlockEntry block = NDS.JIT.LookUpBlock(0, FastBlockLookup,
+                 instrAddr - FastBlockLookupStart, instrAddr);
+             if (block)
+-                ARM_Dispatch(this, block);
++                ARM_Dispatch(this, block, NDS.JIT.Memory.FastMemStart(0));
+             else
+                 NDS.JIT.CompileBlock(this);
+ 
+@@ -772,7 +772,7 @@ void ARMv4::Execute()
+             JitBlockEntry block = NDS.JIT.LookUpBlock(1, FastBlockLookup,
+                 instrAddr - FastBlockLookupStart, instrAddr);
+             if (block)
+-                ARM_Dispatch(this, block);
++                ARM_Dispatch(this, block, NDS.JIT.Memory.FastMemStart(1));
+             else
+                 NDS.JIT.CompileBlock(this);
+ 
+diff --git a/src/ARMJIT.h b/src/ARMJIT.h
+index 4a9b85f..b19996b 100644
+--- a/src/ARMJIT.h
++++ b/src/ARMJIT.h
+@@ -191,8 +191,9 @@ public:
+ };
+ }
+ 
+-// Defined in assembly
+-extern "C" void ARM_Dispatch(melonDS::ARM* cpu, melonDS::JitBlockEntry entry);
++// Defined in assembly. fastMem: the CPU's fast memory base (ARMJIT_Memory::FastMemStart); the AArch64 one puts it
++// in x26 for the block (patch 0024: blocks have no entry prologue setting it)
++extern "C" void ARM_Dispatch(melonDS::ARM* cpu, melonDS::JitBlockEntry entry, void* fastMem);
+ #else
+ namespace melonDS
+ {
+diff --git a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp
+index dc546df..998d455 100644
+--- a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp
++++ b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.cpp
+@@ -280,6 +280,7 @@ Compiler::Compiler(melonDS::NDS& nds) : Arm64Gen::ARM64XEmitter(), NDS(nds)
+         OptExitPC = OptExitStub && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOEXITPC") && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOLINK");   // (ExitCheckPC)
+         OptSelfLoop = OptExitPC && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOSELFLOOP");
+         OptIrqChain = OptExitStub && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOIRQCHAIN");
++        OptNoPrologue = OptFastEntry && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOENTRYX26");
+         OptKeepFlags = !old && !getenv("MELONDS_JIT_NOKEEPFLAGS");
+         // LOOPREGS only with MELONDS_JIT_LOOPREGS=1: on an RG DS Plus, HeartGold (USA) goes to a black screen at its
+         // first overworld frame with it (frame 1200 of tools/device/hgquick.sh's walk), and fine with it off alone.
+@@ -305,7 +306,7 @@ Compiler::Compiler(melonDS::NDS& nds) : Arm64Gen::ARM64XEmitter(), NDS(nds)
+             u32 n = 1;
+             for (int hw = 1; hw < 4; hw++)
+                 n += ((base >> (16 * hw)) & 0xFFFF) != 0;
+-            EntrySkip[num] = OptFastEntry ? 4 * n : 0;
++            EntrySkip[num] = (OptFastEntry && !OptNoPrologue) ? 4 * n : 0;
+         }
+     }
+ 
+@@ -1422,7 +1423,10 @@ JitBlockEntry Compiler::CompileBlock(ARM* cpu, bool thumb, FetchedInstr instrs[]
+ 
+     KnownCodeValid = false;
+     if (OptFastEntry)
+-        Comp_EntryPrologue();
++    {
++        if (!OptNoPrologue)
++            Comp_EntryPrologue();
++    }
+     else if (hasMemInstr)
+         MOVP2R(RMemBase, Num == 0 ? NDS.JIT.Memory.FastMem9Start : NDS.JIT.Memory.FastMem7Start);
+ 
+diff --git a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h
+index bfeb825..20bfbfc 100644
+--- a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h
++++ b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Compiler.h
+@@ -284,6 +284,8 @@ public:
+     bool OptExitStub = true;      // NOEXITSTUB: shorter exit stubs, and no CPSR store when RCPSR is unchanged
+     bool OptExitPC = true;        // NOEXITPC: a constant exit's R15 stored by the exit stub, from a literal
+     bool OptSelfLoop = true;      // NOSELFLOOP: an exit back to its own block's start does the checks inline
++    bool OptNoPrologue = true;    // NOENTRYX26 (patch 0024): no FASTENTRY prologue in the blocks: ARM_Dispatch sets x26,
++                                  // and everything else that enters a block comes from a block of the same CPU
+     bool OptIrqChain = true;      // NOIRQCHAIN (patch 0022): the exit stubs go on into the next block when the only
+                                   // stop reason is an IRQ that CPSR.I masks (the loop's TriggerIRQ would do nothing)
+     bool OptLoopRegs = false;     // LOOPREGS=1 (off by default): a block that loops back to its own start keeps the guest registers
+diff --git a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Linkage.S b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Linkage.S
+index 40a70f4..5ef70da 100644
+--- a/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Linkage.S
++++ b/src/ARMJIT_A64/ARMJIT_Linkage.S
+@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ ARM_Dispatch:
+     stp x25, x26, [sp, #48]
+     stp x27, x28, [sp, #64]
+     stp x29, x30, [sp, #80]
++    mov x26, x2     // the CPU's fast memory base (patch 0024: no entry prologue in the blocks)
+ 
+     // block linking: link the exit that just came back here (its slot in melonds_jit_link) to this block
+ #ifdef __APPLE__
+@@ -49,7 +50,7 @@ ARM_Dispatch:
+     ldr x2, [x2, :lo12:melonds_jit_link]
+ #endif
+     cbz x2, 1f
+-    stp x0, x1, [sp, #-16]!
++    stp x0, x1, [sp, #-16]!       // (x26 is callee-saved: it survives the call)
+ #ifdef __APPLE__
+     bl _melonds_jit_link_pending
+ #else
+diff --git a/src/ARMJIT_Memory.h b/src/ARMJIT_Memory.h
+index a1116ce..8895084 100644
+--- a/src/ARMJIT_Memory.h
++++ b/src/ARMJIT_Memory.h
+@@ -161,6 +161,8 @@ public:
+ 
+     static u32 PageSize;
+     static u32 PageShift;
++    // a CPU's fast memory base, for ARM_Dispatch's x26 (patch 0024)
++    void* FastMemStart(u32 num) const noexcept { return num ? FastMem7Start : FastMem9Start; }
+ private:
+     friend class Compiler;
+     struct Mapping
+diff --git a/src/NDS.cpp b/src/NDS.cpp
+index 48dc0c7..2f4f4b4 100644
+--- a/src/NDS.cpp
++++ b/src/NDS.cpp
+@@ -1297,7 +1297,7 @@ template <u32 num, typename CPU>
+         // LookUpBlock
+         const u64 entry = cpu.FastBlockLookup[offset / 2];
+         if (entry >> 32 == (instrAddr | num)) [[likely]]
+-            ARM_Dispatch(&cpu, (JitBlockEntry)(rxBase + (u32)entry));
++            ARM_Dispatch(&cpu, (JitBlockEntry)(rxBase + (u32)entry), nds.JIT.Memory.FastMemStart(num));
+         else
+         {
+             nds.JIT.CompileBlock(&cpu);
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
